Z||000021||thomas_l||11-07-2001||02:06 PM||||Like all new things, the whining will subside once everyone gets used to it. The trick with this (new) type of search is to use the boolean operators and parentheses wisely.<P>Artherd is right: this new search is very Google-like. You can't sort by date and you can't group a phrase with quotes. But lots of people still use Google because it will sort by relevance - providing your query is detailed enough to screen out the junk you don't want. Thus bringing the good stuff to the top.<P>Garbage In = Garbage Out||||reg||14
